WEBVTT

00:01:46.850 --> 00:01:48.790
This is amazing!

00:01:48.790 --> 00:01:51.410
This is it! This feeling!

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.130
We can definitely win with this!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.060
Haru's songs truly are great!

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:59.550
Each and every sound is so full of happiness.

00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:01.260
Your songs shine brighter and brighter.

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:04.000
Nanami, you did well.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.600
Good work.

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.600
Leave the rest to us.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:11.610
Yes! I really appreciate it.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.110
I see you're all working hard.

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:17.280
We've been working hard too.

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.380
Are these our stage clothes?

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:22.990
Amazing!

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.690
I love this green.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.390
Let me know if there's anything about them that bothers you, and I'll fix it.

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:32.710
You did all of this for us.

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.710
Thank you.

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:38.760
We wanted to help in some way.
 Let us know if you need anything.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:42.530
Tomo, Mr. Tsukimiya.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:45.740
Okay, we'll meet those expectations!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:47.550
Let's give it our best!

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:49.800
I'm so excited!

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:51.210
I know, right?

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.780
That's great. They look like they're having fun.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:58.650
Maybe we should see if we can get more group work.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:02.750
But we work alone primarily.

00:03:02.750 --> 00:03:07.200
I know, but it'd be fun for the four of us to work together.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:11.620
We sing together sometimes, when the president orders us to do so.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:13.550
What good will getting more group work do?

00:03:13.550 --> 00:03:16.730
What? Ran-Ran, you might say that...

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:20.130
But you actually like Quartet Night, don't you?

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:23.590
We had fun singing "Poison Kiss."

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:27.740
I think the four of us actually get along pretty well.

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:32.770
You've got to be kidding. I hate working with others.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:39.420
Let's take it from the top again.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.450
They're at it again.

00:03:56.440 --> 00:03:57.610
Huh?

00:04:04.100 --> 00:04:06.300
Stop, stop!

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.350
What are you doing?

00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:11.290
Huh? What do you mean?

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:16.340
Don't give me that! You're not following the choreography at all!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:18.430
Try it again.

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:19.610
Okay.

00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.740
What?

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.410
That, that right there!

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:38.460
What's that weird spinning dance you're doing?

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:40.580
How rude!

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:44.420
This is a traditional sacred dance of Agnapolis.

00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:47.550
It's a dance for the muses, the Agnadance.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:51.010
Agnadance?

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.560
I see.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:57.300
Um, why are you doing that dance now?

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.470
I'm sorry. It's not on purpose.

00:05:00.470 --> 00:05:01.540
It's just out of habit...

00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:02.770
What?!

00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:04.000
Out of habit?!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:08.420
Did you always do that dance back in your country?

00:05:08.420 --> 00:05:08.810
Yes.

00:05:10.070 --> 00:05:14.120
The prince of Agnapolis sings more than he speaks.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.670
He begins dancing as soon as he is old enough.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:22.430
<i>Wonderful, my prince! Very good!</i>

00:05:22.430 --> 00:05:24.930
<i>Yes, very good!</i>

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:27.610
Everything is for the muses.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:37.730
So for me, there is no dance but the Agnadance.

00:05:38.740 --> 00:05:40.970
What? Seriously?

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:46.480
Habits established at a young age can be difficult to break.

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:54.150
So, the Agnadance has been carved deeply into Ceci's mind and body...

00:05:55.790 --> 00:05:58.920
Our song is amazing now with the addition of Cecil.

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.160
I never thought we'd have trouble with the dancing.

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:06.210
In any case, we need you to be able to dance...

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:08.330
I'll teach you!

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.580
First of all, forget about moving your hands.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:13.100
Let's make sure you're thoroughly familiar

00:06:13.100 --> 00:06:14.440
with just the movements of your feet.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.840
Shou, thank you.

00:06:19.780 --> 00:06:22.260
Okay, let's start from the count.

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:22.850
Okay.

00:06:22.850 --> 00:06:24.200
Left foot first.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:31.410
Five, four, three, two, one.

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:33.080
Don't get flustered.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.830
That's it, slowly.

00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:37.800
Calm down. Good, that's it.

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.080
Shou.

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:40.430
At first, they didn't get along at all.

00:06:39.780 --> 00:06:40.890
Don't spin!

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:44.980
Surprisingly, people like that sometimes end up understanding one another better than others.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:46.400
I see.

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.350
Come on. We should practice as well.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.210
Yes.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:50.210
Yeah.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:54.490
I came here thinking I could teach them to dance,

00:06:54.490 --> 00:06:56.590
but it looks like they don't need me.

00:06:57.230 --> 00:07:00.440
I have my hands full teaching Aijima.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:06.220
How are they going to be ready in time?

00:07:06.220 --> 00:07:08.360
At this rate, their breakup is assured.

00:07:09.410 --> 00:07:14.370
What's wrong with you, Ai-Ai? You don't usually worry about others.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:20.880
They can make the impossible possible.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:22.830
Doesn't it seem that way?

00:07:23.730 --> 00:07:25.070
What are you talking about?

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.080
I believe in them.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:30.250
Believe?

00:07:53.190 --> 00:07:55.270
<i>I believe in them.</i>

00:07:56.330 --> 00:08:00.060
The result is already apparent from the data.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:03.280
How can Reiji believe in them?

00:08:05.020 --> 00:08:09.880
<i>What's wrong with you, Ai-Ai? You don't usually worry about others.</i>

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:13.620
Worry?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.830
<i>I'm interested in them as research subjects, but...</i>

00:08:19.050 --> 00:08:24.480
Me, worried? About them?

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.380
What is this?

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:52.380
<i>What is that feeling?</i>

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:58.210
<i>I can't believe there's music that
 resonates with my soul besides rock.</i>

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.190
Ran-Ran, what are you doing?

00:09:03.540 --> 00:09:07.170
Why do you look after them every day?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:07.940
What?

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.680
I haven't done anything.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:12.740
I thought I could help them out.

00:09:12.740 --> 00:09:16.080
What's this? Ran-Ran, you're worried about your juniors?

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.440
I'm kidding. I'm kidding.

00:09:21.150 --> 00:09:25.460
Ran-Ran, why don't you give what I mentioned before some serious thought?

00:09:25.460 --> 00:09:29.010
<i>That's great. They look like they're having fun.</i>

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:32.780
<i>Maybe we should see if we can get more group work.</i>

00:09:34.110 --> 00:09:35.470
Are you stupid?

00:09:35.860 --> 00:09:40.950
Don't you think it's wonderful to feel the passion of your associates up close?

00:09:40.950 --> 00:09:42.070
This is absurd.

00:09:43.490 --> 00:09:46.100
I'll pass. I don't plan on working with anyone.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.310
Ran-Ran.

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:58.100
Huh? Ai.

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.830
Are you already finished with your work?

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:03.940
Yeah.

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:08.630
Is something wrong? You seem down.

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:10.830
What are you talking about?

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:13.500
More importantly, you don't have much time before your performance.

00:10:13.920 --> 00:10:15.550
Come on, practice.

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:16.670
Okay...

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:19.240
What's his deal?

00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:29.240
Mikaze.

00:10:35.950 --> 00:10:36.650
Kurosaki.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:42.660
Have you noticed that Mikaze has been acting strangely?

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:44.110
What?

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.900
He's been watching ST☆RISH practice this whole time.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.130
So what? What about it?

00:10:49.130 --> 00:10:52.740
The president didn't even tell him to do it.

00:10:53.470 --> 00:10:55.180
Don't you think it's strange?

00:10:56.260 --> 00:11:00.510
Strange things have been happening since we heard that song...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.560
What are you talking about?

00:11:08.160 --> 00:11:10.100
Didn't you feel it as well?

00:11:10.540 --> 00:11:11.760
That song...

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.730
There is something extraordinary about their song.

00:11:16.530 --> 00:11:18.650
Those who heard that song...

00:11:18.650 --> 00:11:24.070
No, those who have come in contact with
 them may experience some kind of change.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:27.540
Without realizing it themselves too.

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.950
Well, I'm unaffected though.

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:32.670
It will be trying for the ignorant.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.920
Something's wrong with Ai and Reiji.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:45.090
<i>Can't the same be said of you, Kurosaki?</i>

00:11:51.830 --> 00:11:52.730
<i>Kurosaki...</i>

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:57.120
<i>Sorry, but I'm quitting the band.</i>

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:58.680
<i>Sorry, Kurosaki.</i>

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:01.380
<i>Hey, what about the concert?</i>

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:04.310
<i>Find some new members.</i>

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.900
<i>We said we'd be friends no matter what!</i>

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.180
<i>Wait, guys!</i>

00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:54.290
<i>Everyone believes in me.</i>

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.830
<i>There's no way I could be affected.</i>

00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.910
We didn't need to worry about him.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.040
That's great.

00:13:41.510 --> 00:13:43.570
Natsuki?! Why are you here?

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.510
The same reason you're here, Shou.

00:13:47.510 --> 00:13:50.210
I was worried about Cecil, so I came to check up on him.

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:52.190
I see.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:54.920
If we all go together, we'll draw too much attention.

00:13:54.920 --> 00:13:56.900
Who cares?

00:13:56.900 --> 00:13:58.290
What?!

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.310
Shou?

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:00.690
Shinomiya?

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:01.920
Guys.

00:14:01.920 --> 00:14:03.020
What are you doing?

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:06.690
We were worried about Cecil...

00:14:06.690 --> 00:14:11.400
Just so you know, we did not arrange to come together.

00:14:11.890 --> 00:14:14.740
We just happened to run into each other on the way here.

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.380
When I tried to leave, Tokiya followed me.

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:22.400
What are you talking about? I planned to come all along.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:25.810
What? You changed in a hurry.

00:14:25.810 --> 00:14:30.010
For us to gather in the middle of the night like this...

00:14:31.030 --> 00:14:33.390
It must mean we're all close friends.

00:14:38.500 --> 00:14:40.390
Cecil's working hard.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:43.330
Tomorrow is finally the day.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:48.340
Yeah. Let's hope his hard work is rewarded.

00:14:48.340 --> 00:14:51.740
We have done our best and must now leave the rest to providence.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.410
Yes.

00:14:53.410 --> 00:14:54.500
Yes.

00:14:57.540 --> 00:14:59.080
Their performance is tomorrow.

00:14:59.480 --> 00:15:01.140
How can they win?

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.920
There must be a way.

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:10.490
<i>What's wrong with you, Ai-Ai? You don't usually worry about others.</i>

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.470
<i>I believe in them.</i>

00:15:16.210 --> 00:15:17.700
Believe?

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:21.620
<i>They can make the impossible possible.</i>

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.050
<i>Doesn't it seem that way?</i>

00:15:23.760 --> 00:15:27.580
I don't understand what that means...

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:36.780
<i>I know, but it'd be fun for the four of us to work together.</i>

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:41.460
<i>I think the four of us actually get along pretty well.</i>

00:15:57.860 --> 00:16:01.130
Ladies and gentlemen, the day has finally come...

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:06.240
The rare title granted when a brilliant idol appears,

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:09.660
the Uta☆Prince Brand New Award!

00:16:09.660 --> 00:16:13.080
It's finally starting!

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:15.820
Cecil, how are you feeling? Are you okay?

00:16:15.820 --> 00:16:20.040
Yes, I've completely suppressed the Agnadance!

00:16:20.040 --> 00:16:22.800
Really? That's great!

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:23.570
Yes!

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:27.880
Huh?

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:30.430
He hasn't suppressed it at all!

00:16:30.430 --> 00:16:35.810
Don't worry. This dance is a prayer to the muses.

00:16:35.810 --> 00:16:39.910
I'm praying for us to put on a great performance.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:42.850
Let's believe.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:44.750
We have to believe.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:45.850
Let's.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:49.830
That's the program.

00:16:49.830 --> 00:16:52.470
Okay. I look forward to working with you.

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:10.500
Meeting you now must be fate. Good.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:15.790
How does it feel to wait for the dissolution of ST☆RISH?

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:20.740
After all, we're going to win. Right, Kira?

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:21.950
Yes.

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:27.660
And you'll happily become our composer. Isn't that great?

00:17:29.020 --> 00:17:30.450
Excuse me.

00:17:30.860 --> 00:17:32.130
Hold on.

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:37.360
Don't be like that. Come with us, and we'll let you watch us rehearse.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:41.000
Please move.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.240
You look great when you're upset.

00:17:46.170 --> 00:17:50.790
Come with us. We'll show you a fantastic dream.

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.220
Quit acting so disgracefully.

00:17:59.270 --> 00:18:00.690
Kurosaki.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.660
Kurosaki Ranmaru.

00:18:03.660 --> 00:18:05.630
Settle it through your song.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.900
Things have already been settled.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:12.230
See you later.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:17.540
Come on, let's get this rehearsal done.

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:21.440
Kurosaki. Um...

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.890
Hurry up and go.

00:18:24.390 --> 00:18:26.190
Thank you very much.

00:18:26.190 --> 00:18:27.400
Goodbye.

00:18:32.640 --> 00:18:33.460
Wait.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:39.860
What are friends to you?

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:41.030
What?

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:55.470
To me, friends are people who feel each other's passion up close.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:19:02.200
<i>I think it's wonderful to feel the passion of your associates up close.</i>

00:19:15.410 --> 00:19:16.400
<i>I...</i>

00:19:20.690 --> 00:19:24.820
Who will be awarded the Uta☆Prince Award?

00:19:24.820 --> 00:19:29.030
Will it be the top new idol group, and favored to win, HE☆VENS?

00:19:29.030 --> 00:19:32.170
Or will it be ST☆RISH, who came into the limelight like a comet

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:36.110
with their song, "Maji LOVE 1000%"?

00:19:37.270 --> 00:19:40.280
You don't want to miss this battle!

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:43.570
Yeah, ST☆RISH!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:44.790
You can do it!

00:19:50.850 --> 00:19:54.660
Our commentator is Hyuga Ryuya,

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:56.610
well known for his role on the drama, <i>Prince of Fighting</i>!

00:19:56.610 --> 00:19:57.840
Thanks for having me.

00:19:58.420 --> 00:20:01.740
In the committee's seats are prominent figures from various fields

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:04.490
serving as members of the Uta☆Pri committee.

00:20:10.590 --> 00:20:14.710
What's this? Raging Otori and Shining Saotome!

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:16.790
The presidents of both agencies have arrived!

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:22.260
The time has come to finally settle their long-standing feud!

00:20:23.290 --> 00:20:26.700
Let's go, Saotome! Give up!

00:20:26.980 --> 00:20:29.700
Come, HE☆VENS!

00:20:31.790 --> 00:20:34.940
The greatest warriors of music!

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.440
Raging storm!

00:22:31.690 --> 00:22:34.360
<i>A-Amazing...</i>

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:09.350
I wish that everyone's feelings will reach.

00:24:09.850 --> 00:24:11.020
UtaPri!
